  "text": "Breadcrumbs List.\nShow Truncated Breadcrumbs.\nHome\nNgā akoranga | Study\nInternational students\nYou are currently on:\nMeet our international students\npage. Open sub navigation overlay.\nMeet our international students\nOur international students and alumni from around the world share their experiences of studying at the University of Auckland, why they chose to study here and how it has helped set them up for future success.\nAlif Hafizi\nAgustin Soto\nBoorani Moorthy\nChristine Mak\nDean Lin\nDilani Goonetilleke\nEva Li (Yutong)\nEddie Yang\nEvelyn Guo\nFabian Rabenda\nFredrick William Hennings\nGuy Patrick\nHenry Oh\nHoang Ha Chi Nguyen\nJeongmin Won\nKate Wood\nThiraphop Rangsisukanon\nSahan Jayasuriya\nSamantha Poh\nYixin Wang\nZhanjie Gan\nZhen Zhang\nZoea Chen\nZhanjie Gan\nZhanjie is pursuing a Bachelor of Education in TESOL (Teaching English to Speakers of Other Languages) and hopes to build a career in bilingual education.\nMeet Zhanjie\nGraduate stories\nHear from our international alumni and find out what exciting and fulfilling careers they have gone on to pursue.\nDiscover more\nScholarship student stories\nLearn about international students who have received scholarships to study at the University of Auckland.\nCheck them out\nPhD student stories\nHear from international students who are studying for their PhD at the University of Auckland.\nLearn more\nStudy Abroad student stories\nRead about students who have studied abroad with us and check out their blogs.\nRead more\nBoorani Moorthy\nBoorani returned to study after a few years in the construction industry. She is pursuing a Master of Engineering Studies in Construction Management.\nMeet Boorani\nThiraphop Rangsisukanon\nThiraphop is a Thai international student completing a Bachelor of Health Science with the goal of a career in health management.\nMeet Thiraphop\nPlay Video\nNorwegian nursing students talk about Auckland\nInternational nursing students Hanna Johre and Martine Brevik explain why they chose to study at our Faculty of Medical and Health Sciences.\nStudent stories from Latin America\nRead stories in Spanish from our Latin American students at the University.\nLee mas\nInternational student videos\nStudents from a range of countries talk about their time in Auckland.\nGo to our Youtube channel",
